The Go rendering: a command declaring one iota group per use the class does not
follow. A pointer to a struct holding one type reaches encoding/json through a
function of the program that hands its empty-interface parameter on; one type is
decoded by a generic helper into a value of its type parameter; one is filled
through a function-valued parameter; one is a type argument of a generic function
in a module outside the target; one is asserted out of an interface value; one
is read through unsafe.Pointer; one is converted from a float; one is held by an
unexported field of a struct a pointer to which goes to encoding/json.Marshal.

A second file covers more shapes: a pointer to a struct whose unexported embedded
field is one type, a promoted exported field, a receive-only, a send-only and a
bidirectional channel handed to a module outside the target, a pointer inside an
error, a pointer put into a slice of empty interfaces, a struct field, an element
assigned, a returned value and a sent value of the empty interface, pointer
conversions both ways, a function result reached by reflection, a type-switch
case, a write through unsafe.Pointer and a map key decoded by encoding/json.
Every group ends with a member that ends.go names by comparison, and the member
before it is the subject.

